docs {
  Not a notifications endpoint — this is the action that produces one, kept here
  so the whole pipeline can be exercised from a single folder.

  Creating an enquiry writes the row and a MassTransit outbox row in one
  transaction, so the event is exactly as durable as the enquiry itself. The
  notification service consumes it, resolves everyone holding
  admission.enquiryfollowup.get, writes one row per recipient, then pushes over
  SignalR.

  Two things to expect:

  - The creator is excluded. Logging in as the only permission holder and
    creating an enquiry produces no notification for yourself — that is correct
    behaviour, not a failure. Use a second account to see it arrive.
  - Delivery is not instant. The outbox sweeps on an interval, so allow a few
    seconds before checking Get Unread Count.

  The GUIDs above are from the local dev database and will not exist in Stage.
  Replace them from Admissions Master Data and Academic lookups for that
  environment.
}
